From: jt914 <josephtso914@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Offer no save-and-fill dialog without a tab

On a card form while no card is saved, Chrome's autofill dropdown offers
"Save card for faster checkout", whose dialog, SaveAndFillViewDesktop,
CHECKs for the tab interface of its web contents. EngineCore's tabs have
none, so choosing the entry crashed the browser. The save and fill manager
is now null for a web contents without a tab interface, as it is on
Android, and every caller already reads null as "do not offer".
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/chrome_payments_autofill_client.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/chrome_payments_autofill_client.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/chrome_payments_autofill_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/autofill/payments/chrome_payments_autofill_client.cc
@@ -1198,6 +1198,11 @@ SaveAndFillManager* ChromePaymentsAutofillClient::GetSaveAndFillManager() {
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   return nullptr;
 #else
+  // The save and fill dialog needs the tab interface, which EngineCore's
+  // tabs lack. Without a manager the entry is not offered.
+  if (!tabs::TabInterface::MaybeGetFromContents(web_contents())) {
+    return nullptr;
+  }
   return save_and_fill_manager_.get();
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 }
